Subject: [PATCH 0/4] Show what GDI draws outside the destination rect of a D3D present.

A windowed D3D9 Present with a destination rect only replaces that part of
the window on Windows, what GDI draws in the rest stays visible. With
wined3d on OpenGL the client surface covers the whole client area instead,
and the parts that are never presented to are black. MikuMikuDance presents
its preview to a part of its main window only, and its panels around it,
drawn with GDI, were black.

wined3d now tells win32u the part of the window it presents to, with a new
Wine escape, and the drivers only show that part of the client surface.
Drivers that draw the client surfaces over the window surface (Android) also
keep the client area in it, so that it shows what GDI drew there.

Tested with a D3D9 test on X11 (Xvfb, llvmpipe): presenting a part of a
window with GDI drawn bands and child windows left all the bands black with
the DISCARD and FLIP swap effects, they now show, and presenting the whole
window is unchanged. d3d9:visual and d3d9:d3d9ex pass, d3d9:device has one
failure, as Xvfb only has one display mode.

chatgptyukkuri (4):
  win32u: Don't clip the client area out of the window surface without
    PutImage.
  win32u: Add the part of the client area presented to to client
    surfaces.
  winex11: Only show the presented part of client surfaces.
  wined3d: Tell win32u which part of the window a GL swapchain presents
    to.

